{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1344197-peach-crossover-self-insert","id":1344197,"title":"[PEACH] Crossover Self-Insert","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-28T08:39:59-07:00","id":1344197,"title":"[PEACH] Crossover Self-Insert","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> We are toying with the idea of a Self-Insert chronicle, in which the players will be themselves as they are in the real world and their win condition will be to &quot;fix the world&quot; or at least prevent the end of it.<br /> <br /> Assume that collectively we own all the books of the oWoD, and we will use 20th anniversary rules (V20+V20DA, M20, W20, Wr20, C20).<br /> <br /> Characters will have the PC's real life stats (whatever they end up being, merits and flaws included), their supernatural template of choice (all are Mages), 7 Background dots (only to get supernatural Backgrounds, nothing social), Willpower at 5, no freebies (so Arete is 1 and so are the Spheres), the year is 1997.<ul><li><b>What are easy/fast, non-evil power-ups for them?</b></li> <li><b>What are their better/faster/safer bets to stop the worst case scenarios of the Time of Judgement?</b> We were thinking:</li> </ul><br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>London</b>. Find <i>Charon</i>/<i>Charles Andersen</i>, ally with him.</li> <li><b>Worldwide</b>. Find <i>Lyla Yvonne Tzigano</i> and use her help to ally with <i>Lilith</i>.</li> <li><b>Worldwide</b>. Find <i>The Perfect Metis</i>, and help him deal with many Apocalypse scenarios (this has to wait until 1999).</li> <li><b>Hong Kong</b>. Kill <i>Oliver Thrace</i> (avoid one of the worst Time of Judgement scenarios).</li> <li><b>Switzerland</b>. Ally with <i>Horus</i>, use his help to find and kill <i>Eurydice </i>(avoid two Time of Judgement scenarios).</li> <li><b>Finland</b>. Kill <i>Louhi </i>(avoid part of one of the worst Gehenna scenarios), should use <i>Horus' </i>(point 5) help to achieve this</li> <li><b>Russia</b>. Ally with <i>Durga Syn</i>, use her help to redeem <i>Shazear </i>and help <i>Vasilisa </i>kill <i>Baba Yaga</i>, find <i>Koschei</i>'s Soul Egg and throw it into Malfeas.</li> <li><b>Kaymakli</b>. Kill <i>Augustus Giovanni</i> (he is not that strong)</li> <li><b>Berlin</b>. Ally with <i>Ankla Hotep</i>, use his godly stats and disciplines to fight the Antediluvians when they appear.</li> <li><b>Worldwide</b>. Find <i>The Shaper</i> Antediluvian and ally with her.</li> <li><b>Transylvania</b>. IF [<i>Tzimisce</i>] is moving, release <i>Kupala </i>(as idiotic as it sounds) and let them kill each other (avoid part of two of the worse Gehenna scenarios).</li> <li><b>Worldwide</b>. IF <i>Caine </i>and the Antediluvians are appearing, use <i>Lilith</i>'s (point 2), <i>Ankla Hotep</i>'s (point 9) and <i>The Shaper'</i>s (point 10) help to destroy them (so most Gehenna scenarios never occur, and without <i>Caine</i> in most cases all vampires are destroyed).</li> <li><b>Yellow Springs</b>. Ally with <i>Chan </i>and <i>Lei Zu</i>, kill <i>Yu Huang</i>, make <i>Lei Zu</i> queen. Use <i>Charon </i>help (point 1) to achieve all of this.</li> <li><b>Yomi Wan</b>. Help <i>Voormas </i>kill <i>Tou Mu</i>, ally with him, and let him and <i>The Unnamed</i> fight each other; destroy the winner (two of the worse Ascension scenarios averted).</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Up to point 5, those are <i>relatively </i>easy (with a bit of experience, even up to point 8): they could still die horribly, but those do not require a lot of personal power, more a lot of meta-knowledge. After that, things are downright suicidal.<br /> <br /> We would love any suggestions on both questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-04-2020, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link"